tion"} "\n" [:p {} "The 1936 Olympic gymnastics competitions were held at the " [:a {:href "/venues/329"} "Dietrich-Eckart-Freilichtbühne"] ", in the Reichssportfeld. This was an outdoor venue, which was common for gymnastics in that era, but it would be the last time Olympic gymnastics was conducted outdoors. After the " [:a {:href "/editions/10/sports/GAR"} "1932 programme"] ", which included some unusual, American-oriented events such as " [:a {:href "/results/70110"} "rope climbing"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/70112"} "tumbling"] ", and " [:a {:href "/results/70111"} "club swinging"] ", the 1936 gymnastics programme returned to the men’s standard of a " [:a {:href "/results/70114"} "team"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/70113"} "individual all-around"] ", with six apparatus events. Women had competed in a " [:a {:href "/results/70088"} "team all-around at Amsterdam in 1928"] ", but had no gymnastics events at the 1932 Olympics. However, in Berlin, the " [:a {:href "/results/70127"} "women’s team all-around"] " was returned to the Olympic Programme."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Germany and Switzerland dominated the events, winning 22 of the 28 medals, with Germany winning 13 and Switzerland nine medals. Germany won six of the nine events. They were led by " [:a {:href "/athletes/30249"} "Konrad Frey"] ", who won six medals and three golds, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/30304"} "Alfred Schwarzmann"] ", who won five medals and the individual all-around."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70113"} "Individual All-Around, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "10 – 11 August 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "111"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70114"} "Team All-Around, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympi